BT /F1 15 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 708 Tm (Retention for report exports) Tj /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 688 Tm (Status: proposed) Tj /F1 15 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 656 Tm (Context) Tj /F1 13 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 636 Tm (The export worker writes each report export to object storage as a CSV file.) Tj /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 616 Tm (Nothing deletes them, so storage holds every export since launch.) Tj /F1 15 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 584 Tm (Requirements) Tj /F1 13 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 564 Tm (R1. An export is deleted when its retention period ends.) Tj /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 544 Tm (The period depends on the account plan, as the table below gives it.) Tj /F1 13 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 524 Tm (R2. A customer can download an export until it is deleted.) Tj /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 504 Tm (R3. Every deletion is written to the audit log before the export is removed.) Tj /F1 13 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 484 Tm (Plan Retention) Tj /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 464 Tm (Free 30 days) Tj /F1 13 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 444 Tm (Team 90 days) Tj /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 424 Tm (Enterprise 365 days) Tj /F1 15 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 392 Tm (Design) Tj /F1 13 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 372 Tm (A nightly sweep selects the exports whose retention period has ended.) Tj /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 352 Tm (For each, it writes an audit entry, deletes the object, then deletes the row.) Tj /F1 13 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 332 Tm (A row whose object is already gone is deleted without an error.) Tj /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 312 Tm (So a sweep that stops partway and runs again leaves the same state.) Tj /F1 13 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 292 Tm (Enterprise exports are kept for 90 days, the same as Team.) Tj /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 272 Tm (So the sweep needs only two retention periods.) Tj /F1 13 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 252 Tm (The sweep skips every account with a legal hold.) Tj ET
